  "summary": "Validate Windows recovery-lock ownership by safe live native file identity without reading through a second exclusively locked handle; retain the bounded marker and existing liveness/deletion guards.",
  "behavior": [
    "On Windows only, compare simultaneously open file handles via exact already-locked same-file 1.0.6. Never unlock, use unsafe code, enable nightly APIs, disable features or weaken liveness/foreign-file checks.",
    "Read the bounded marker through the owner handle on Windows. Unix marker/device/inode checks remain active and byte-equivalent.",
    "Reopen and compare the named Windows file after its link/type metadata check to detect replacement.",
    "Adapt the existing book partial-commit assertion to Rust Debug-escaped Windows paths; require the exact one-element completed prefix and retain all failure/unchanged-file/staging assertions.",
    "Apply after immutable original archive, branding patch and original protected-file verification. The original branding patch, all legal files and all unrelated source remain byte-identical."
  ],
